### `me` raised to `exp` with raw IEEE 754 propagation (inf/NaN on overflow/domain). Wraps
### `rf_f16_pow`.
routine F16.pow_unchecked(exp: F16) -> F16
  return F16.from_bits(bits: C::rf_f16_pow(base: me.to_bits(), exp: exp.to_bits()))

### Raises this value to `exp`, checked: crashes on a non-finite result (overflow -> inf, domain ->
### NaN). Use `pow_unchecked` for raw IEEE 754 propagation.
### :param exp: The exponent applied to `me`.
### :returns: `me` raised to `exp` (always finite).
routine F16.pow!(exp: F16) -> F16
  var rr = me.pow_unchecked(exp: exp)
  if rr.is_finite()
    return rr
  if rr.is_nan()
    throw NumericDomainError(description: "domain error: no real result")
  throw NumericOverflowError(description: "overflow: out of range")

